{"t":1793436573695,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.847a1488c7b13091f639b46dbc0d2074ce9c067f.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.5,29.08],[-81.69,29.32],[-81.57,29.35],[-81.42,29.1],[-81.5,29.08]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.847a1488c7b13091f639b46dbc0d2074ce9c067f.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.847a1488c7b13091f639b46dbc0d2074ce9c067f.001.1","areaDesc":"Lake, FL; Volusia, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012069","012127"],"UGC":["FLC069","FLC127"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC069","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC127"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b17471914b8565dfa339052a1a87ce08a6538769.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b17471914b8565dfa339052a1a87ce08a6538769.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-10-30T11:15:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-10-30T21:02:00-04:00","effective":"2026-10-30T21:02:00-04:00","onset":"2026-10-30T21:02:00-04:00","expires":"2026-10-31T12:00:00-04:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 30 at 9:02PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.\n\n.Persistent northeast winds and downstream tidal effects on the St\nJohn River are slowing flow at Astor.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 3.5 feet, Canals have overflowed into yards. Homes on\nor near Wildhog, Bonnet and Snail roads become inaccessible with\nseveral inches of water inside homes along the river and canals.\nDocks at Astor Bridge marina and throughout Astor are completely\nsubmerged. Bartram Rd and Holiday Circle are inaccessible with\nyards completely submerged. Clair Street is inaccessible. Roads\nflooded in South Moon Fish Camp, docks and yards at condominiums on\nJuno Trail and water breaches the sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 PM EDT Friday the stage was 3.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 PM EDT Friday was 3.7 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 3.6 feet.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Saturday afternoon at noon EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 310102"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2a9e7fac7b5c5ad78bd2e1cf1fc774708f767f2.002.1,2026-10-29T21:03:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1840da910b02e49f40570094c2ce4d840da0f7e7.002.1,2026-10-29T09:16:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c7fdda2979f0f8f25569f6cde0da27cc8358a302.001.1,2026-10-28T21:31:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9aeb600074fc600db94b853bee79670c058b0e1e.001.1,2026-10-28T08:58:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840